## Lore

The Overlords are Kydians, the Splugorth''s main military force and a large share of all their minions. Their home world was dying of its own fertility: multiple births, maturity at fourteen and a six month gestation had choked the planet with trillions of people, pollution, starvation and violence, with mandatory euthanasia at 45 and extinction two generations away. The Splugorth offered rescue in exchange for eternal service, and 53,000 years later the Kydians still count it a bargain. They enjoy health and prosperity they never knew, and the losses of endless conquest seem a fair price for the combat and adventure they love.

Kydians are huge, super strong and tireless, ideal infantry. Freed from their crowded world they have become even tempered, obedient and law-abiding, yet aggressive in battle. They are fair strategists but rarely rise to command, bowing to the High Lords and other minions. The Splugorth deliberately teach them only what a soldier needs, and most know little of science, magic or technology, relying on their masters for everything.

## Appearance

A tall, bulky, powerfully built humanoid, 8 to 10 feet tall and 400 to 600 lbs, with grey to purple-grey skin, black eyes sunk deep in their sockets and a pair of small horns on the chin. Usually clad in bio-wizard body armor and augmented by bio-wizard devices and implants. To everyone''s surprise, the Kydians'' included, they live about 140 years.

## Renegades

A rogue Overlord is a rarity: the Kydians see the Splugorth as their saviors. A player character must be a renegade, seen by its own kind as an ingrate or a psychotic, and is attacked, captured or killed on sight by Splugorth minions. Capture means hard labor, the arena or experimentation.

## Equipment

Overlords use almost anything but favor Splugorth bio-technology, and otherwise love high-powered variable lasers, particle beam rifles and rail guns. Standard issue: the Staff of Pacification, Overlord power armor, one purirobe, two clotrobes, and two further bio-wizard devices, weapons or microbes; police also carry two zombitrons. Only the highest ranking officers receive a rune weapon, never a greatest one. Other bio-wizard gear available by assignment includes Eylor floating eyes, the Eylor Helm of Omnipotence and Psionic Rod (officers only), the Eylor Seeker-Hunter, forearm plasma blaster, helmet laser, jolt gun, plasma rifle, psi-interrogator, microbes, the Staffs of Power, Eylor and All Seeing, symbiotic organisms and weapon modifications, and the telepathic holographic imager.

## GM Notes

The book calls the Overlord a rarity as a player character, to start at first or second level. NPC Overlords average level 1D4+2.
